    "marks": 4,
    "model": "Example: a beginner learning the basketball free throw cannot yet feel what is wrong with their shot.\nThe coach watches and gives one precise correction straight after the shot, such as keep the elbow under the ball, which is extrinsic feedback.\nThe player can apply that single cue on the next attempt, and as their skill improves the coach gives less feedback so the player relies more on their own feel.",
