    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Pathway 1: formal club-school links with a shared coach.\nA local club provides a qualified coach to deliver a block of PE lessons or an after-school session in the school, ending with an open invitation to a club session and a named contact. This removes the barrier of turning up alone to an unfamiliar club, and gives the school coaching expertise it may lack.\nPathway 2: shared use of school and community facilities.\nThe school opens its hall, pitches and pool to local clubs and families outside school hours under a written agreement, and the club helps pay for upkeep. This gives young people a familiar setting to try new activities and makes the move from school to community sport easier.",
