    "model": "A vector quantity has both magnitude and direction, for example a velocity of 5m/s towards the goal.\nA scalar quantity has magnitude only, for example the speed of 8.13m/s in the 400m race.\nIn sport, a scalar such as distance tells how far an athlete has travelled, while a vector such as displacement also tells how far they are from the start in a specific direction, which matters in games where position relative to a target is important.",
