    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Role 1: enforcing the rules and ensuring fair play.\nIn hurling the referee blows the whistle for a foul, awards a free and shows a card when the offence requires it, so the game is controlled and fair.\nRole 2: judging and scoring performance.\nIn gymnastics the judges award marks for difficulty and execution against the code of points, so each athlete's result is accurate and consistent.",
