    "model": "Physical activity: Hurling.\nFootwear: Moulded or studded boots suited to the pitch allow a player to grip, accelerate and turn without slipping, whereas unsuitable or poorly fitting boots cause blisters and increase the risk of ankle and knee injury.\nProtective clothing: A helmet with a face guard and gum shield protects the head, face and teeth from a sliotar struck at high speed.\nClothing: Light, loose and breathable clothing lets the player move freely and stay cool, whereas clothing that restricts movement or traps heat reduces performance.\nImportance: Suitable attire protects the player from injury and allows them to perform at their best.",
