    "model": "HRF component: Flexibility.\nPRF component: Balance.\nActivity: A dynamic single-leg clock reach routine.\nThe athlete stands on one leg with a slight bend at the knee and imagines a clock face on the floor around them.\nThey slowly reach the free leg out to 12, 3, 6 and 9 o'clock, touching the floor lightly at each point, and return to the start position without putting the foot down.\nFlexibility is trained because the hip, groin and hamstring muscles move through a large range of motion at each reach.\nBalance is trained because the athlete must hold a stable position on one leg while the centre of mass shifts with each reach.",
