    "model": "Raise: Five to eight minutes of low-intensity continuous movement, such as jogging or skipping, to increase heart rate, body temperature and blood flow to the muscles.\nActivate and mobilise: Activate the specific muscles the activity relies on, such as the glutes and hamstrings, and move the joints through the ranges used in the activity, such as leg swings and arm circles.\nPotentiate: Gradually increase intensity with activity-specific movements, such as practising the skill at increasing speed, to prepare the body for maximal effort.",
